Sublime Point Maintenance Corridor B-7, 2 hours before midnight, December 25th
\f1\i0 \
The insertion goes better than expected. Smythe's intelligence proves accurate, guiding them through a service tunnel that Dunhilton's forces haven't discovered. Inside Sublime Point, the effects of the temporal distortions are immediately apparent. Lights flicker between normal illumination and strange colors that shouldn't exist. Occasionally, objects phase partially out of existence, then reappear seconds later.\
"The effects are getting worse," Smythe whispers, consulting a device that resembles a pocket watch with too many hands. "We have less than two hours before critical mass."\
Jones activates the biosignature detector. It immediately points deeper into the facility. "Hardman is in the central laboratory complex."\
"As expected," Smythe nods. "I'll head to the security center to gather intel and possibly disable some systems to hamper Dunhilton's forces when they arrive. We'll rendezvous at the north service elevator in ninety minutes."\
Jones doesn't particularly expect to see Smythe again\'97the man will either betray him or get himself killed\'97but he nods agreement. As Smythe limps away, Jones moves stealthily toward the central labs.\
The corridors of Sublime Point become increasingly unstable as he approaches the center of the facility. Twice he has to flatten himself against walls as security teams run past, not noticing him due to his stealth suit or perhaps because they're phasing partially into other realities.\
Near the laboratory entrance, Jones encounters a temporal anomaly that ages him twenty years in thirty seconds, then reverts him back. The experience leaves him disoriented and, strangely, more contemplative than before. For a brief moment, he had seen through older, wiser eyes\'97eyes that questioned whether eliminating Hardman was truly the solution to anything.\
Shaking off these unsettling thoughts, Jones slips into the observation gallery above the main laboratory. Below, he sees the Gyges Discs arranged in a pentagram formation, pulsing with energy. Scientists scurry about, making adjustments as reality warps around them.\
And there, at the center of it all, is Gerry Hardman, deep in conversation with Eloise Shakti and a heavily pregnant woman who must be Sarah Jacobson.\
Jones raises his weapon, finally ready to eliminate Jihad Man once and for all, when a hand clamps down on his shoulder.\
"I wouldn't do that if I were you," says a voice.\
Jones whirls to find himself face to face with... Gerry Hardman.\
"But you're\'97" Jones looks back at the laboratory, where Hardman still stands with Eloise and Sarah. "How can you be in two places at once?"\
"Temporal duplication," Hardman explains calmly. "A side effect of the experiments. That's not actually me down there\'97it's me from six hours ago. Just as I met myself from six hours in the future earlier today. It's all getting rather complicated."\
Jones keeps his weapon trained on Hardman. "You're working with Dunhilton. You betrayed everything you swore to protect."\
Hardman sighs. "Is that what Smythe told you? He's partially right, but missing crucial context. Yes, I've been working with Dunhilton\'97to feed him false information. To keep him distracted while we prepare for what's coming."\
"Which is what, exactly?"\
"A rebirth," Hardman says simply. "Something impossible is about to happen, Jones. Sarah's child will be born at the exact moment of dimensional convergence. The result will reshape reality itself\'97hopefully for the better."\
"You expect me to believe you're working for the greater good?" Jones scoffs.\
"I expect you to look at the evidence before you make decisions that can't be unmade." Hardman gestures to a nearby monitor showing Dunhilton's forces gathering outside Sublime Point. "He's not here to save anyone. He wants to control the convergence, to reshape reality in his image. We're trying to ensure that doesn't happen."\
Jones's detector suddenly beeps wildly. Multiple Hardman signatures appear throughout the facility\'97past, present, and future versions all converging.\
"It's starting," Hardman says grimly. "Reality is fracturing. Soon, Sarah will go into labor, and everything changes. You have a choice to make, Jones. Right now."\
Before Jones can respond, the observation gallery door bursts open. Haloren Smythe staggers in, bleeding from a head wound.\
"Jones! Don't listen to him!" Smythe gasps. "Dunhilton's forces are inside already. They're heading for the\'97"\
An explosion rocks the facility, cutting him off. Below, the lab erupts into chaos as security alarms blare.\
Through the smoke and confusion, Jones sees a figure enter the lab that makes his blood run cold: CEO Dunhilton himself, flanked by elite security forces, moving directly toward Sarah Jacobson.\
In that moment, as reality itself begins to come apart at the seams, Agent Ajent Jones finds the strains of "You'll Never Walk Alone" playing unbidden in his mind. And for the first time in his life, he knows exactly what he needs to do.\
The universe is about to collapse, and Agent Jones\'97gospel-infected, reality-warped, and finally seeing clearly\'97prepares to make his stand at Sublime Point.\
